-- Adds every degree from the uploaded "CareerGuide -- Degree Master List"
-- PDF that isn't already one of the 10 rows V44 added (b-tech, diploma,
-- b-ed, mba, mca, b-sc, b-com, bba, phd, certificate) -- 124 new rows
-- across the PDF's ~20 category groupings (Engineering & Technology,
-- Computer Science & IT, Science, Commerce & Finance, Arts & Humanities,
-- Economics, Law, Medicine & Healthcare, Pharmacy, Nursing, Allied
-- Healthcare, Education, Architecture & Planning, Design & Fine Arts,
-- Media & Communication, Agriculture, Hospitality & Tourism, Sports).
--
-- The PDF's own "Modeling Note" page confirms this catalog's existing
-- shape is the intended one: Degree is meant to be an independent entity
-- that connects directly to a Discipline/Career (its own example shows one
-- degree, BTech, covering multiple disciplines) rather than being nested
-- under Specialization or Job Role -- exactly what V44/V51's
-- degrees/career_degrees tables already do. This migration is data-only:
-- it adds the missing Degree catalog rows themselves, matching V44's
-- original scope, but does NOT link any of them into career_degrees --
-- that's a deliberate separate step, same as how V47 (single-degree
-- linking) followed V44 (degree catalog) by three migrations, and V51
-- (many-to-many linking) is itself a separate migration from V44.
--
-- Naming/slug notes: a handful of PDF abbreviations collide with plain
-- English words if used as a bare slug ("me", "be", "march", "med"), so
-- those become b-eng/m-eng/m-arch/m-ed instead (titles still show the
-- PDF's own short form, e.g. "BE", "ME"). "Master of Surgery (MS)" is
-- slugged ms-surgery rather than the very generic "ms". Every other slug
-- is the PDF's own abbreviation, lowercased, hyphenating only where the
-- source already writes it as "B.X"/"M.X" (matching V44's b-tech/b-sc/
-- b-com/b-ed convention) rather than a run-together acronym like MBA/MBBS.
--
-- Descriptions and preparation_strategy text are newly written for this
-- migration (the PDF itself is only a title list, one page per category,
-- plus the modeling note above) -- each aims to be genuinely informative
-- rather than filler, but at this volume (124 rows) they're necessarily
-- more concise than V44's original 10 hand-crafted entries; several
-- closely-related variants (e.g. the five B.Sc/M.Sc CS&IT majors, or the
-- five AYUSH medicine degrees) intentionally share a similar structure
-- since the underlying degrees themselves are structurally similar (same
-- duration, same entrance-exam route, differing only in subject focus).
--
-- degree_exams/degree_skills/degree_resources (V44) are deliberately left
-- empty for all 124 -- populating real, specific entrance-exam/skill/
-- resource relations for each would need the same kind of grounded,
-- verifiable research V44's original 10 had, which this migration doesn't
-- have a source for; better empty than guessed.

